    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in the outfield as **Kyle Tucker** (73.89) and **Andy Pages** (66.95) stand out as our most reliable offensive drivers. Both benefit from a favorable matchup against Gallen, whose 4.36 xERA provides a high-ceiling environment for our power bats. While **Kyle Tucker** draws the premium score by anchoring the middle of the order, **Andy Pages** remains a high-floor play, leveraging his spot in the two-hole and neutral platoon splits to maximize scoring potential. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.53) remains a must-start despite a stiff matchup against Holmes, as his elite xwOBA remains the backbone of our run production in the heart of the order.\n\nTactical edge-seeking remains critical, particularly with **Sam Antonacci** (58.72) capitalizing on a strong leadoff position and a favorable platoon profile against Bradley. Conversely, we are mitigating risk against elite arms; both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Miguel Andujar** face xERAs below 3.00 today. **Miguel Andujar** specifically requires monitoring, as his score is propped up by a platoon advantage against S\u00e1nchez that barely offsets the significant drop-off caused by the pitcher's elite skill level. The most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo** (51.16), who finished just shy of the active rotation; while his power metrics are enticing, he was edged out by **Josh Jung** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who offer more favorable lineup placement and safer efficiency floors in their respective matchups. We continue to prioritize preserving our limited game caps, keeping players like **Jackson Merrill** and **Brayan Rocchio** benched, as their current projections fell below our required 40.0 efficiency threshold given the caliber of the opposing arms.",
